  "profileEditSnsPostsTokenConsentTitle": "Deposit your login key with RASQ",
  "profileEditSnsPostsTokenConsentMessage": "To show {account}'s posts on your account page, **your login key (access token) for this SNS will be deposited with RASQ's server**.\n\n• Your \"Public\" and \"Home (unlisted)\" posts become **viewable by anyone on your RASQ account page**. \"Home\" is not followers-only.\n• Followers-only / specified users and DMs / local-only / posts with unknown visibility aren't imported.\n• The key is used only to read your posts. It isn't used for actions like posting or following, or for any other purpose.\n• The key is stored encrypted with the server's key (RASQ's server can decrypt it). It isn't returned to the app or anyone else.\n• Turning this switch off immediately deletes the deposited key and fetched posts.\n\nWith this key, the account can be operated. If you're concerned, you can revoke this key (token) from the SNS's settings even after depositing it.",
