  "settingsPagesAboutCookiesTitle": "About cookies",
  "settingsPagesAboutCookiesSection1Title": "Cookies",
  "settingsPagesAboutCookiesText1": "The iOS, Android, and desktop apps do not use cookies to communicate with the RASQ server. Communication with the RASQ server uses a device token (Authorization header), and each SNS access token is stored in a secure area on your device.",
  "settingsPagesAboutCookiesText2": "Ads in the iOS and Android apps (Google AdMob) use your device's advertising ID instead of cookies. On the Google consent screen shown the first time, you can choose whether to allow personalized ads.",
  "settingsPagesAboutCookiesText3": "On the web version and on RASQ's public profile and post web pages, Google uses cookies for ads (Google AdSense). Ad cookies are handled according to Google's policies.",
  "settingsPagesAboutCookiesText4": "When you open an SNS's web version or sign-up page in the in-app browser, that SNS's cookie policy applies.",
